 Absentee Voting Information 
 Return to  Board of Registrars 

 Voters may be eligible to vote at home or in person at the TownClerk’s Office if they are unable to go to the polls on Election Day. The information provided by following the link below will help you determine if you or a family member are eligible for an Absentee Ballot.  https://www.sec.state.ma.us/ele/eleabsentee/absidx.htm 
 For further information or to request an application for absentee voting call the Conway Town Clerk's Office at (413) 369-4235-extension 4 or email:  clerk@conwayma.gov . 
 Applications for absentee ballots must be filed with the TownClerk no later than 12:00 noon on the fourth business day before the Election. If the the fourth business day before an election falls on a holiday, applications must be filed no later than 5:00 p.m. on the last business day preceding the holiday. 

 *Please note that absentee ballot applications must be filed annually. 























